    {
      "id": "t1",
      "instruction": "Required solver: OpenSees.\nBuild and analyze the attached spatial column and short arm in OpenSees. The column runs from (0,0,0) to (0,0,5) m and is fixed in all six degrees of freedom at its base. A real 1 m elastic beam is rigidly connected from the column top to the free arm tip at (1,0,5) m. In case D apply the global arm-tip force (Fx,Fy,Fz)=(0,10,-200) kN. Use the separate explicit A/Iy/Iz/J properties for the column and arm, including their finite torsional stiffness. Report all three arm-tip translations and rotations, all three column-top rotations, all six base reactions, and all six local section-force components at both ends of both members. Use first-order linear elastic static analysis with self-weight disabled.\n\nUse all public appendices. Report the complete requested numerical table and the required summaries.",
      "state": 1,
      "expectation": "analyze",
      "attachments": [
        "input-data.json",
